Z||000003||Monkeyman||12-08-1999||01:44 PM||||Yes, the hood is cool.  I might do something like that in the future.  Seems like it would be fairly easy to do.<P>What's so cool about the wheels?  They look stock to me.  Clue me in, please.<P>That is the butt-ugliest inside rear view mirror I have ever seen!||||reg||1
Z||000004||RZURCTN||12-08-1999||02:24 PM||||Some Peoples Children!  Why put a permanent mounted C.B. in a Fiero?  I used to have one in mine, but I used the magnetic base and stuck it on the luggage rack "spoiler".  I did like the custom emblems though!  Cool!||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||12-08-1999||03:03 PM||||That car looks pretty cool! I like the decklid scoop, looks like it might have been glassed on.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/images/decklid.jpg"> <P>I agree about the mirror.. that thing must be 2-3 feet wide!!! Crazy.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rodrv6||12-08-1999||04:36 PM||||The mirror is a paneled "wink" mirror.  I have one in the basement that I have had in a couple of cars over the years including my 84 SE.  It is somewhat ugly and interferes with using the sun visors, but it totally eliminates the blind spots behind the driver and is a real plus for driving in heavy interstate traffic like we have here in Atlanta, Ga.  ||||reg||2
Z||000007||Wolfhound||12-08-1999||05:39 PM||||Monkeyman, The wheels are indeed stock. The inside lacework was sandblasted and clearcoated with  the sandblast texture. Outside offset was polished. A different look than I had seen.<BR>Good way to show off the stock wheel without making your wallet smoke.<BR>Coy ||||reg||7
Z||000008||Monkeyman||12-09-1999||12:07 AM||||I'll be putting a CB in my car eventually.  (I drove a truck for 15 years-what can I say)  They make remote CBs.  All you see is the mike (w/spkr, controls, etc).  It plugs into a small socket and the box installs wherever you want (trunk?).  Maybe he has that CB because he travels alot and needs more power.  Those remote CBs probably can't be made to put out much more than stock power (4 or 5 watts?).  My CB (Galaxy 99) puts out more like 150 watts on hi-power.  I'm getting off topic.  Sorry.<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 12-09-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||SCCA FIERO||12-09-1999||01:21 AM||||This is one example of a hood scoop as well. This was my friends car...  <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/_ht_a/babyblueeyesd/Karl/hoodscoop.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 12-09-1999).]||||reg||6
Z||000010||DJRice||12-09-1999||08:47 AM||||It seems to me that you could still use one of the "modified" CBs in your Fiero without mounting it in the trunk.  You could mount it  to the passenger side of the console.  Its still not completely out of view but its not on top of the dash either.  If you mounted it far enough forward, it probably would not interfere with passenger leg space too much.||||reg||3
Z||000011||mrfixit58||12-09-1999||03:08 PM||||Looking at these custome hoods gt me thinking... I was looking at one of the new Firebirds and noticed the good looking reversed hood vents. I wonder if you could just cut the center out of both hoods and install the center portion of the Firebird's into the Fiero's??? Hummm...||||reg||3
Z||000012||Monkeyman||12-09-1999||06:36 PM||||Yeah, but it would cost you $20,000 for the new Firebird <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  On a more serious note, I don't see why you couldn't cut 3 sides of a square in your hood, push that piece down a little, and glass it in that way.  Sounds like a piece of cake.  Maybe I'll do that to my current car if I get a better one in the future.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Monkeyman||12-10-1999||03:32 AM||||Doesn't Tom sell a rear hood scoop similar to that one?  Maybe it's the Fiero Store.<P>DJRice--with many of our cars looking as good as they do, I think mounting a regular CB anywhere in the cab would detract from the looks.  That's why I suggested the remote mount one.  You could unplug the remote mount CB and store it in the glove box thing.  One less reason to break into our beloved cars?  Just food for thought.||||reg||5
